# Only hand-written seed inputs are checked in as reference corpus.
# Auto-discovered inputs from `cargo fuzz run` are local-only.
*
!.gitignore

# Phase 123-07 (PKGX-02): this target's seeds are DELIBERATELY not checked in.
#
# The two inputs that make invariant 2 ("every blob's content hashes to its own
# key") reachable are derived from plan 04's golden corpus at
# `crates/pmcp-package/tests/golden_fixtures/artifact_tar_v1/conformant.tar`.
# Checking copies in here would give that fixture a second source of truth,
# which is exactly the drift hazard `artifact_tar_v1/README.md` exists to
# prevent — a copy can only ever agree with whatever produced it.
#
# Regenerate them instead (run from the repository root):
#
#   mkdir -p cargo-pmcp/fuzz/corpus/fuzz_package_artifact
#   cp crates/pmcp-package/tests/golden_fixtures/artifact_tar_v1/conformant.tar \
#      cargo-pmcp/fuzz/corpus/fuzz_package_artifact/seed_conformant.tar
#   python3 - <<'PY'
#   src = "crates/pmcp-package/tests/golden_fixtures/artifact_tar_v1/conformant.tar"
#   dst = "cargo-pmcp/fuzz/corpus/fuzz_package_artifact/seed_layer_byte_flipped.tar"
#   b = bytearray(open(src, "rb").read())
#   # 4608 is the data offset of the 44-byte envelope LAYER blob
#   # (blobs/sha256/74e664...). Flipping one byte there leaves the entry LENGTH
#   # unchanged, so the descriptor size check still passes and the archive is
#   # refused for exactly one reason: the blob no longer hashes to its own name.
#   b[4618] ^= 0x01
#   open(dst, "wb").write(bytes(b))
#   PY
#
# Arbitrary bytes will not stumble onto a well-framed OCI layout inside a
# bounded campaign, so without these seeds the three invariants are asserted
# over an input set that never reaches them.
